1	//! The work run's detach/status/wait lifecycle (design v1): `--detach` starts the run in a
2	//! background process (the record's `run.json` in state `running` carries the background's
3	//! options wire, as the consult detach's status file does), `--status` prints every work run
4	//! of the task and `--wait` blocks for it. A small module of its own rather than a reuse of
5	//! `crate::consult::detach`: the consult machinery is welded to `Options` (its `DetachArgs`
6	//! wire mirrors every consult flag) and to the consult status-file shape; the work record
7	//! already is the status file here. The Windows spawn (a `CreateProcessW` that holds none of
8	//! the caller's handles) IS reused from the consult detach.
